IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-seat`

-- Worked cases for tas-seat.l4: at least one case for every question, and a case the encoding does not cover (an explicit NOTHING) for each question that can answer NOTHING.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the cited section, with a calendar for the weekdays, before the module was run.
-- Weekdays used below: Thursday 1 January 2026, Friday 2 January, Saturday 3 January, Sunday 4 January, Monday 5 January, Tuesday 6 January, Thursday 8 January, Saturday 10 January, Sunday 11 January, Monday 12 January;
-- Sunday 25 January, Monday 26 January, Tuesday 27 January, Saturday 31 January, Sunday 1 February, Monday 2 February 2026; Sunday 15 February 2026, Monday 16 February 2026;
-- Sunday 16 July 2028, Monday 17 July 2028; Tuesday 15 January 2030; Sunday 1 September 2030, Monday 2 September 2030.
-- Fixture dates are values chosen for the test; the Act does not state them:
-- section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 is taken to have commenced on 1 January 1982.
-- Where a question needs a date that the rule does not read for the facts given, 1 January 2026 is filled in.

`no days to exclude` MEANS EMPTY
`Monday 26 January 2026 is a public holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 26 1 2026)
`Monday 5 January 2026 is a public holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 5 1 2026)
`Saturday 10 January 2026 is a public holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 10 1 2026)
`Thursday 1 January 2026 is a public holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 1 1 2026)
`Monday 16 February 2026 is a public holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 16 2 2026)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `When an Act or an instrument comes into operation and stops operating (ss 9, 14)`

-- s 9(3): assent on 10 March 2026, on or after the commencement of section 8 of the 1981 Act, no contrary intention: the fourteenth day after 10 March is 24 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 24 3 2026)
-- s 9(3) boundary: assent on the day section 8 commenced is "on or after"; the fourteenth day after 1 January 1982 is 15 January 1982.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 1982)
-- s 9(2) boundary: assent the day before section 8 commenced: the day of assent.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 31 12 1981) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 1981)
-- s 9(2): assent on 5 June 1979: the day of assent.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 5 6 1979) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 5 6 1979)
-- s 9(4): reserved on 5 March 2026, proclamation published on 20 April 2026: the day after, 21 April 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 21 4 2026)
-- Outside the encoding: the Act shows a contrary intention, so the day is whatever that Act says, and this Act does not say.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Outside the encoding: the Act commences on a day to be proclaimed, and s 9(3A) fixes only the commencement provision and the short title.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 9(5): an instrument expressed to commence on 1 July 2026 takes effect immediately on the expiration of 30 June, that is at the first moment of 1 July.
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument in operation at the moment` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Act or instrument in operation at the moment` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE)
-- s 14(2): it continues until the last moment of the day it expires on, 31 December 2026; the first moment of 1 January 2027 is outside.
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument in operation at the moment` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the Act or instrument in operation at the moment` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument in operation at the moment` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `When a right or a liability ends (ss 15, 16, 18A)`

-- s 15(1): the repealed provisions remain in force until the substituted provisions come into operation on 1 July 2026: in force on 30 June, not on 1 July.
#ASSERT `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(1) "Where" fails: no repeal with substituted provisions.
#ASSERT `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day` FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 16(1) and (2) closing words: after a repeal or expiry, a legal proceeding may still be started or continued, unless the contrary is expressly provided.
#ASSERT `May I still bring a legal proceeding after a repeal or expiry` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I still bring a legal proceeding after a repeal or expiry` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I still bring a legal proceeding after a repeal or expiry` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 18A: temporary enactment expired on 30 June 2026, the continuing Bill was assented to on 15 August 2026; nobody is liable for what they did between the two dates, both counted in.
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 29 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 16 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18A "upon receiving the Governor's assent": no assent yet, so the relief does not apply.
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE FALSE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: what was done was not contrary to the temporary enactment, so the section's relief has nothing to do.
#ASSERT `Am I free from punishment between expiry and assent` TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Counting my time (s 29)`

-- s 29(1): 30 days from 1 January 2026 end on 31 January 2026, a Saturday; Saturday is not an excluded day, so the day stands.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 31 1 2026
-- s 29(3)(a): 23 days from 2 January end on Sunday 25 January; the next day not an excluded day is Monday 26 January.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 2 1 2026) 23 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 26 1 2026
-- s 29(3)(a): the same with Monday 26 January a public holiday: Tuesday 27 January.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 2 1 2026) 23 `Monday 26 January 2026 is a public holiday` EQUALS Date 27 1 2026
-- s 29(3)(a): 31 days from 1 January end on Sunday 1 February; Monday 2 February.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 1 1 2026) 31 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
-- s 29(6): a time of 3 days, excluded days not reckoned: from Friday 2 January, Saturday 3 January is the first day, Sunday 4 January is not reckoned, Monday 5 January the second, Tuesday 6 January the third.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 2 1 2026) 3 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 6 1 2026
-- s 29(6): a time of 1 day from Saturday 3 January: Sunday is not reckoned, so Monday 5 January.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 3 1 2026) 1 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 5 1 2026
-- the edge of s 29(6): 6 days from Thursday 1 January: Friday 2, Saturday 3, Monday 5, Tuesday 6, Wednesday 7 and Thursday 8 January (Sunday 4 January is not reckoned), so 8 January.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 1 1 2026) 6 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 8 1 2026
-- just past it, 7 days from Thursday 1 January end on Thursday 8 January, which is not an excluded day (s 29(1)).
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 1 1 2026) 7 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 8 1 2026

-- s 29(3)(a) and s 46: 36 calendar months from 16 July 2025 end on Sunday 16 July 2028, so Monday 17 July 2028.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 16 7 2025) 36 `no days to exclude` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
-- 60 calendar months from 15 January 2025 end on Tuesday 15 January 2030.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 15 1 2025) 60 `no days to exclude` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- 60 calendar months from 1 September 2025 end on Sunday 1 September 2030, so Monday 2 September 2030.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 1 9 2025) 60 `no days to exclude` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
-- one calendar month from 15 January 2026 ends on Sunday 15 February, so Monday 16 February; with that Monday a public holiday, Tuesday 17 February.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 15 1 2026) 1 `no days to exclude` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 2 2026)
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 15 1 2026) 1 `Monday 16 February 2026 is a public holiday` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 2 2026)
-- Outside the encoding: February 2026 has no 31st day, and the Act does not say what corresponds.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 `no days to exclude` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in calendar months` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 `no days to exclude` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Outside the encoding: the Act does not say what a year is, so a number of years gives no answer.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in years` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By which day must I act in years` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 29(1) backwards: 30 days before 31 January 2026 begin on Thursday 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 31 1 2026) 30 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
-- s 29(3)(b): with 1 January a public holiday, the act is in due time only if done on the next day before that is not an excluded day: Wednesday 31 December 2025.
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 31 1 2026) 30 `Thursday 1 January 2026 is a public holiday` EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
-- s 29(3)(b): 7 days before Sunday 11 January fall on Sunday 4 January; the next day before is Saturday 3 January.
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 11 1 2026) 7 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 3 1 2026
-- s 29(6), a time of not more than 6 days: 3 days before Monday 12 January: Sunday 11 January is not reckoned; Saturday 10, Friday 9 and Thursday 8 January are the three days.
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 12 1 2026) 3 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 8 1 2026
-- with Saturday 10 January a public holiday, it is not reckoned either: Friday 9, Thursday 8 and Wednesday 7 January.
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 12 1 2026) 3 `Saturday 10 January 2026 is a public holiday` EQUALS Date 7 1 2026
-- the edge of s 29(6): 6 days before Tuesday 13 January: Monday 12 January is the first, Sunday 11 January is not reckoned, then Saturday 10, Friday 9, Thursday 8 and Wednesday 7 January, and Tuesday 6 January is the sixth.
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 13 1 2026) 6 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 6 1 2026
-- just past it, 7 days before Tuesday 13 January fall on Tuesday 6 January, which is not an excluded day (s 29(1)).
#ASSERT `On or before which day must I act, counting backwards` (Date 13 1 2026) 7 `no days to exclude` EQUALS Date 6 1 2026

-- s 29(2): 5 clear days after 1 January 2026 are 2 to 6 January, so the act may first be done on 7 January.
#ASSERT `On which day may I first act after clear days` (Date 1 1 2026) 5 EQUALS Date 7 1 2026
-- 1 clear day after 31 December 2025 is 1 January 2026, so 2 January.
#ASSERT `On which day may I first act after clear days` (Date 31 12 2025) 1 EQUALS Date 2 1 2026

-- s 29(2): 5 clear days before 20 January 2026 are 15 to 19 January, so the latest day is 14 January.
#ASSERT `On which day must I act at the latest before clear days` (Date 20 1 2026) 5 EQUALS Date 14 1 2026
-- 1 clear day before 1 January 2026 is 31 December 2025, so 30 December 2025.
#ASSERT `On which day must I act at the latest before clear days` (Date 1 1 2026) 1 EQUALS Date 30 12 2025

-- s 29(3): a Sunday is an excluded day; a listed holiday is; a Saturday and an ordinary Monday are not.
#ASSERT `Is the day one that does not count` (Date 4 1 2026) `no days to exclude`
#ASSERT `Is the day one that does not count` (Date 26 1 2026) `Monday 26 January 2026 is a public holiday`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the day one that does not count` (Date 31 1 2026) `no days to exclude`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the day one that does not count` (Date 5 1 2026) `no days to exclude`)

-- s 29(4): the last day, Saturday 31 January, falls on a day the office is not open; the next day it is open is Monday 2 February.
#ASSERT `On which day may I file or register` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE (Date 2 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- the office is open on the last day: that day.
#ASSERT `On which day may I file or register` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- Outside the encoding: the office is closed and the next open day given is not later than the last day.
#ASSERT `On which day may I file or register` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 29(5): an act directed to be done on Sunday 4 January, a day fixed so that subsection (3) does not apply: Monday 5 January.
#ASSERT `On which day is my act in due time on a particular day` (Date 4 1 2026) TRUE `no days to exclude` EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)
-- with Monday 5 January a public holiday: Tuesday 6 January.
#ASSERT `On which day is my act in due time on a particular day` (Date 4 1 2026) TRUE `Monday 5 January 2026 is a public holiday` EQUALS JUST (Date 6 1 2026)
-- a particular day that is not an excluded day: that day.
#ASSERT `On which day is my act in due time on a particular day` (Date 6 1 2026) TRUE `no days to exclude` EQUALS JUST (Date 6 1 2026)
-- Outside the encoding: subsection (3) is applicable, and s 29(5) speaks only of a day so fixed that it is not.
#ASSERT `On which day is my act in due time on a particular day` (Date 4 1 2026) FALSE `no days to exclude` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Being served with a notice or document (ss 29AB, 30, 30A)`

-- s 29AB(1)(a)(i): a natural person may be served by giving the document to the person.
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 29AB(1)(a)(ii): or by leaving it at, or posting it to, the last known residential or postal address.
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `leaving it at the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `sending it by post to the person's residential or postal address or place or address of business or employment whichever is last known to the server` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 29AB(1)(b): any other person may be served by leaving it at, or posting it to, the principal or registered office.
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `any other person` `leaving it at the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `any other person` `sending it by post to the person's principal or registered office or principal place of business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 29AB(1) "without directing it to be served in a particular manner": the Act directs a manner, so the subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE TRUE `a natural person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 29AB(1) "If an Act authorizes, requires or permits": no such Act.
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` FALSE FALSE `a natural person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: the lists in paragraphs (a) and (b) are not closed with "only".
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `any other person` `giving it to the person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the way I was served one that the Act allows` TRUE FALSE `a natural person` `some other way` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 30(1): properly addressed and posted, postage paid: taken to be served when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post, here 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- Outside the encoding: not properly addressed and posted, or the contrary is proved.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by post` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 30(2)(a): registered post, duly registered: 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by registered post` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- s 30(2)(b): by the certified mail service, with no contrary intention in the Act: 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by registered post` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- Outside the encoding: the certified mail service, but the Act shows a contrary intention; or neither registered nor certified; or the contrary is proved.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by registered post` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by registered post` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to have been served by registered post` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 30A(a): an infringement notice may be served electronically if the recipient consents.
#ASSERT `Can an infringement notice be served on me electronically` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can an infringement notice be served on me electronically` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: the document is not an infringement notice.
#ASSERT `Can an infringement notice be served on me electronically` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 30A(b): taken to be served if sent electronically to an address or number provided for that purpose.
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have been served electronically` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have been served electronically` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the encoding: the document is not an infringement notice.
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have been served electronically` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `When a proclamation or regulation takes effect, and when regulations are void (ss 38A, 47)`

-- s 38A(2)(d)(i): it names 1 September 2026, and is published on 10 August 2026: 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does a proclamation or order-in-council take effect` TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 10 8 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
-- s 38A(2)(d)(ii): it names no day: the day of publication, 10 August 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does a proclamation or order-in-council take effect` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 8 2026) EQUALS Date 10 8 2026

-- s 47(3)(d)(i): the regulations name 1 September 2026, and are published on 10 August 2026: 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day do regulations take effect` TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 10 8 2026) EQUALS Date 1 9 2026
-- s 47(3)(d)(ii): they name no day: the day of publication, 10 August 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day do regulations take effect` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 8 2026) EQUALS Date 10 8 2026

-- s 47(3A)(a), (b) and s 47(3)(a), (b): made on 1 July 2026, published on 22 July 2026, the 21st day after the day they were made: in time, so not void.
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 22 7 2026) (Date 22 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- published on 23 July 2026, the 22nd day: not in time, so void.
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 23 7 2026) (Date 23 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- never published or notified, and the 21 days have run out: void.
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 47(3A)(c): published on 15 July 2026 but expressed to take effect on 1 July 2026, a day preceding publication: void if rights would be prejudiced, or if liabilities would be imposed.
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 15 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 15 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the same, with neither prejudiced rights nor imposed liabilities: the "where" of paragraph (c) fails, so not void.
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 15 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expressed to take effect on the day of publication: not void.
#ASSERT `Are the regulations void` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE (Date 15 7 2026) (Date 15 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
